          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rani Chennamma of Kittur</p>",
            "<p>1824</p>",
            "<p>First armed resistance against British in Karnataka; refused to follow Doctrine of Lapse; fought Thackeray (British Collector); died in captivity 1829</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Sangolli Rayanna</p>",
            "<p>1829–31</p>",
            "<p>Military commander of Rani Chennamma; continued guerrilla warfare; hanged by British at Nandagad in 1831; Karnataka's folk hero</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Surpura (Shorapur) Revolt</p>",
            "<p>1858</p>",
            "<p>Raja Venkatappa Nayaka of Surpura (Yadgir) revolted; part of 1857 Mutiny aftermath in Karnataka</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Nargund Revolt</p>",
            "<p>1858</p>",
            "<p>Bhashkar Rao Bhat Nargundkar revolted; hanged in 1858</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kodagu Resistance</p>",
            "<p>1834</p>",
            "<p>Chikka Viraraja of Kodagu — last king; deposed by British; exiled to Benares</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
