        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Background</strong></p>",
            "<p>Kannada-speaking areas were split across Mysore State, Hyderabad, Bombay, Coorg, Madras and Central Provinces under British</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>States Reorganisation Act 1956</strong></p>",
            "<p>Reorganised states on linguistic basis; all Kannada-speaking regions merged on November 1, 1956</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Renamed Karnataka</strong></p>",
            "<p>Under Chief Minister D. Devaraj Urs, State renamed from Mysore to Karnataka on November 1, 1973</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Ekikarana Samiti</strong></p>",
            "<p>Organisation that led the agitation for Kannada unification; Aluru Venkata Rao &amp; others spearheaded it</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>First CM of Mysore State</strong></p>",
            "<p>S. Nijalingappa (1956–58)</p>"
          ]
        },
